    <page>
  <definition xml:id="poisson-process">
    <title>(2.6-1)</title>
    <statement>
      <p>
         Let the number of occurrences of some
      event in a given continuous interval be counted. Then we have an <fillin characters="50"/>
      with parameter <m>\lambda\gt 0</m> if the following conditions are
      satisfied:
      <ol>
        <li>
          <p>
            The numbers of occurrences in nonoverlapping subintervals are
            independent.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <p>
            The probability of exactly one occurrence in a sufficiently short
            subinterval of length <m>h</m> is approximately <m>\lambda h</m>.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <p>
            The probability of two or more occurrences in a sufficiently short
            subinterval is essentially zero.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      </p>
    </statement>
   </definition>
